# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.pem
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# local editors and tooling
/.vscode/
/.idea/
/.turbo/
/.cache/

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template, which carries no values — only the variable names a
# deployment must set. Lead delivery (src/lib/leadDelivery.ts) refuses to send
# without these, so an operator needs to know they exist.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# local planning notes
/HOMEPAGE_MISSING_PARTS.md

# Private company context — MUST NOT be published.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC (github.com/Bhaveshmeghwal21/pawaac-website), and
# PAWAAC_CONTEXT.md is an internal commercial reference file, not site content.
# Treat it as confidential in full.
#
# This comment used to enumerate the specific categories the file contains, on
# the reasoning that documenting the risk justified the rule. That was
# self-defeating: the list itself was committed to a public repository, so it
# disclosed the substance of what the ignore rule exists to protect. The
# enumeration is removed deliberately — do not restore it. Anyone who needs to
# know what is in the file has the file.
#
# It has never been committed, so ignoring it here is sufficient — no history
# rewrite is needed. CLAUDE.md still references it with `@PAWAAC_CONTEXT.md`,
# which is deliberate: the import simply no-ops in a clone that does not have
# the file, and it documents the intended local setup.
/PAWAAC_CONTEXT.md

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# design-sync (claude.ai/design import) — tooling scratch + generated output.
#
# Widened from three carve-outs to the whole directory. Nothing under src/
# imports anything from it and `next build` succeeds with it untracked, so it is
# not part of the app. The narrower rules left ~19 generated files staged for
# commit: hashed next/font .woff2 subsets, compiled CSS, and duplicate copies of
# components that already live in src/components/ui — the duplicates are the
# real reason to exclude it, since they go stale silently.
/.ds-sync/
/ds-bundle/
/.design-sync/

# Claude Code — share launch.json and settings.json (project dev-server config
# and permissions), keep per-developer overrides local.
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/*.local.json

